# .gitignore

### Go ###
# Compiled Go binaries
# These are generated by `go build` and should not be in source control.
orchestrator/orchestrator_app
renderer/renderer_app
distributor/distributor_app

# General rule for any other local builds you might do
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.zip
.Rhistory
logs/

### Data, Assets, and Generated Files ###
# This is the most important rule. Your Git repository should contain your
# application's CODE, not the DATA it operates on. Customer assets,
# temporary files, and final videos are data, not code.
/data/

### Docker ###
# Ignore local environment files. A .env.example should be committed instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample

### macOS ###
# General OS-specific files
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Thumbnails
._*

### IDEs and Editors ###
# VS Code
.vscode/

# JetBrains (GoLand, etc.)
.idea/

# Sublime Text
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

roadmap.md
node_modules
/work
